<article class="post post-reference">
<header class="post-header">
<h1>The robots.txt guide</h1>
<div class="post-meta">
<p>Last updated <time datetime="2026-10-26">26 October 2026</time></p>
<p><a class="button" href="https://www.example.com/demo/">Book a demo</a></p>
</div>
</header>
<nav class="toc-box" aria-label="Contents">
<p class="toc-title">Contents</p>
<ol class="toc-nested">
<li><a href="#what-robots-txt-does">What robots.txt does</a>
<ol>
<li><a href="#who-reads-it">Who reads it</a></li>
<li><a href="#who-ignores-it">Who ignores it</a></li>
</ol>
</li>
<li><a href="#how-to-write-one">How to write one</a></li>
<li><a href="#how-to-check-it">How to check it</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<div class="post-body">
<aside class="callout callout-summary">
<ul>
<li>robots.txt asks crawlers to stay out of some paths.</li>
<li>It does not hide a page from search results.</li>
</ul>
</aside>
<h2 id="what-robots-txt-does">What robots.txt does <a class="heading-link" href="#what-robots-txt-does" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
<p>It is a plain text file at the root of your site that crawlers read first.</p>
<h3 id="who-reads-it">Who reads it <a class="heading-link" href="#who-reads-it" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>
<p>Search engine crawlers that follow the rules read it before anything else.</p>
<h3 id="who-ignores-it">Who ignores it <a class="heading-link" href="#who-ignores-it" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>
<p>Scrapers that do not follow the rules ignore it.</p>
<h2 id="how-to-write-one">How to write one <a class="heading-link" href="#how-to-write-one" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
<p>Start with one rule per path you want left alone, then list your sitemap, as <a href="/blog/what-a-sitemap-does/">what a sitemap does</a> explains.</p>
<h2 id="how-to-check-it">How to check it <a class="heading-link" href="#how-to-check-it" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
<p>Open the file in a browser at /robots.txt and read each rule aloud.</p>
<aside class="callout callout-note">
<p>Test every change before you publish it. A wrong rule can hide your whole blog.</p>
</aside>

</div>
</article>
